Table~\ref{tab:counterfactual_spatial} reports counterfactual instruction analysis on LIBERO-Spatial (10 tasks).
The effect ordering is identical to LIBERO-Goal: empty $>$ wrong $>$ shuffled $>$ paraphrased, with the same shuffled--paraphrased violation ($\rho = 0.8$).
All effect sizes exceed $d = 0.8$, and cross-task consistency is comparable (CV: $0.06$--$0.10$).
Spatial instructions differ only in prepositions (e.g., ``on the plate'' vs.\ ``in the drawer''); the wrong-task $d = 0.851$ demonstrates that instruction-dominant heads encode fine-grained spatial relations, not merely task identity.

